  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.9.9 — Onboarding overhaul\n\nFirst-run is now a guided wizard instead of a static \"install Ollama, run serve, pull a model, then come back\" panel. The path from `dotnet tool install -g MandoCode` to first chat is auto-detected, auto-recovered, or auto-installed at every step where it's possible.\n\nAdded:\n- Guided wizard auto-fires on first run and via `/setup`. Walks users through Ollama install → daemon start → cloud sign-in → model pick → context size, all from inside the terminal.\n- Auto-install Ollama via `winget` / `brew` / `curl install.sh` with inherited stdio so users see the installer's progress. Falls back to opening ollama.com/download if the install fails.\n- Auto-launch `ollama signin` as a child process — browser opens to confirm, CLI writes the local token automatically. No more \"browser sign-in alone isn't enough\" trap.\n- Auto-launch `ollama serve` when the daemon isn't running, with a Spectre Status spinner showing live progress.\n- 401 auto-recovery on chat — if the daemon returns 401 mid-session, the cloud sign-in walkthrough fires immediately so users don't have to type `/setup`.\n- Trailing-slash heal on the Ollama URL: `http://localhost:11434/` is detected and silently corrected.\n- Wrong-port auto-fallback: when the configured URL fails after `ollama serve` succeeds, the wizard auto-probes `http://localhost:11434` and switches if the daemon is reachable there.\n- PATH-refresh detection on Windows — checks canonical install paths (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Ollama\\ollama.exe`) when `where ollama` fails, so post-install detection works without relaunching.\n- Tiered local-model picker with hardware guidance (qwen3.5 0.8b / 2b / 4b / 9b with VRAM expectations).\n- Cloud upsell: after a local pull, surfaces `minimax-m2.7:cloud` as the more capable option (free with `ollama signin`).\n- Combined cloud/local model picker with `(cloud)` / `(local)` badges. Replaces the old two-step \"Cloud or Local? → list\" flow.\n- New `/model` slash command — quick switch model + context size, skips the rest of `/config`.\n- New `--doctor` CLI flag — non-interactive preflight that prints .NET version, OS, Ollama CLI/daemon status, models pulled, cloud sign-in state.\n- New `<red>` / `<green>` / `<yellow>` / `<cyan>` HTML tag handlers in MarkdownHtmlRenderer for inline color in chat error responses.\n\nUI:\n- k-notation labels in the max-tokens picker (`32k`, `128k`, `200k`) instead of raw token numbers, with current value highlighted at top via `← current` marker.\n- Educational intro on temperature and max-tokens steps — explains what tokens are, the relationship to the model's context window, and per-tier usage examples.\n- VDOM-aware text input for URL entry in `/setup` and `/config` — RazorConsole's `TextInput` instead of Spectre's `TextPrompt` (which dropped keystrokes alongside the live render loop). Pre-filled with current URL (\"press Enter to keep current\").\n- 401 chat errors render the `Error:` header in red and the recommended action in green; backticked `ollama signin` keeps the existing purple inline-code styling.\n\nChanged:\n- Default cloud model bumped from `minimax-m2.5:cloud` → `minimax-m2.7:cloud` (config defaults, README, `/learn`, system prompt).\n- Default `MaxTokens` bumped from 4k → 32k for new installs (existing configs preserved).\n- `MaxMaxTokens` lowered from 256k → 200k after testing showed many cloud models hit a practical limit closer to 200k once system prompts and tool definitions are accounted for. Existing configs with 256k saved get clamped on next load.\n- `/help` table reorganized with `/setup` and `/model` next to `/config` and disambiguated descriptions.\n- 16+ failure messages across the app now consistently point users at `/setup` and/or `/retry`.\n\nFixed:\n- Status-aware model-list fetch with auto-retry — transient `/api/tags` failures no longer misroute users (with pulled models) into the \"no models yet\" flow.\n- Post-pick auth check — pulled cloud models that show in `/api/tags` after sign-out no longer cause the wizard to falsely report \"Setup complete\" before the chat fails with 401.\n- Picked-model validation via `/api/show` before the wizard declares success, surfacing models that listed in `/api/tags` but aren't actually loadable.",
